SPOILER:
Actually that should not be a problem at all:
Just make a shell escape (unix) or save the game (on shitty systems)
Then look at the directory where your level-saves are. 
(On Unix it is most of the times a directory like /usr/games/nethackdir.
 I suggest a shell-script like this:
 cd /usr/games/nethackdir	#or some other directory
 ls -l <your uid*>		#to list only your files
 ls -l bones*			#to list the boones-files)
So you can a) look at the file-sizes of the level-saves: big size means a lot
	      of stuff around that level: i.e. shop, ghost or treasurezoo,etc.
	   b) look at what levels there are bones around.
	      (actually I use to wait at the first levels until someone dies
	      just below me.)
This should help you.
